The '''2015 FIFA Club World Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2015 FIFA Club World Cup]], an [[association football]] tournament hosted by [[Japan]]. It was the 12th final of the [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a [[FIFA]]-organised tournament between the winners of the six continental confederations as well as the host nation's league champions.

The final was contested between Argentine club [[Club Atlético River Plate|River Plate]], representing [[CONMEBOL]] as the reigning champions of the [[Copa Libertadores]] and Spanish club [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]], representing [[UEFA]] as the reigning champions of the [[UEFA Champions League]]. It was played at the [[Nissan Stadium (Yokohama)|International Stadium]] in [[Yokohama]] on 20 December 2015.
Barcelona won the game 3–0 to claim their third FIFA Club World Cup title.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/35141742|title=River Plate 0-3 Barcelona|date=20 December 2015|work=BBC Sport|access-date=21 December 2015}}</ref>	
The win for Barcelona was also their fifth trophy of 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/dec/20/barcelona-river-plate-luis-suarez-club-world-cup|title=Lionel Messi and Luis Suárez fire Barcelona to Club World Cup title|date=20 December 2015|work=Guardian|access-date=21 December 2015}}</ref>

==Background==
===River Plate===
[[Club Atlético River Plate|River Plate]] qualified for the tournament as winners of the [[2015 Copa Libertadores]], following a 3–0 aggregate win against [[Tigres UANL|UANL]] in the [[2015 Copa Libertadores Finals|final]]. This was River Plate's first time competing in the tournament. They have played two times in the [[Intercontinental Cup (1960–2004)|Intercontinental Cup]], the predecessor of the FIFA Club World Cup, with one win ([[1986 Intercontinental Cup|1986]]) and one loss ([[1996 Intercontinental Cup|1996]]). They reached the final after defeating Japanese club [[Sanfrecce Hiroshima]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/dec/16/river-plate-club-world-cup-final-sanfrecce-hiroshima|title = River Plate reach Club World Cup final with victory over Sanfrecce Hiroshima|website = [[TheGuardian.com]]|date = 16 December 2015}}</ref>

===Barcelona===
[[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] qualified for the tournament as winners of the [[2014–15 UEFA Champions League]], following a 3–1 win against [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] in the [[2015 UEFA Champions League Final|final]]. This was Barcelona's fourth time competing in the tournament, after winning twice in [[2009 FIFA Club World Cup|2009]] and [[2011 FIFA Club World Cup|2011]], as well as being runners-up in [[2006 FIFA Club World Championship|2006]]. They have played one time in the [[Intercontinental Cup (1960–2004)|Intercontinental Cup]], with one loss ([[1992 Intercontinental Cup|1992]]). They reached the final after defeating Chinese club [[Guangzhou Evergrande Taobao F.C.|Guangzhou Evergrande]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/35095550|title=Barcelona 3-0 Guangzhou Evergrande|work=BBC Sport}}</ref>

